  "behavior": [
    "Unsigned remainder by a constant power of two lowers to the existing AND path through a private instruction copy.",
    "The bounded 8/16/32/64-bit classifier accepts one and high-bit divisors, including their signed spelling, and rejects zero, nonpowers and out-of-width literals.",
    "Native tests preserve original inputs, scalar values and guards across clobbering calls and skipped branches; three modes run direct/release routes against LLVM.",
    "The unchanged Fibonacci capture passes remainder and now reaches composed-block-call-arg-width."
  ],
  "known_boundaries": [
    "Other divisor forms, signed remainder and widths outside 8/16/32/64 retain existing rules.",
    "Existing AND preservation/home limits remain: a frameless loaded RAX value with a 2^32 divisor rejects; the retained reproducer records that limitation.",
    "Fibonacci still has 24 rejected functions out of 34, no whole object, and zero local whole-program executions. The full authorized plan continues with narrow call arguments/returns, storage and aggregate forms, remaining scalar/memory forms, indirect calls, and native program acceptance."
  ],
